ine the color and column formatting functions that the shared library needs to export, matching the output formatting requirements across utilities.\n\nNow checking the design decisions: D1 correctly enforces the architectural boundary that format can't import from cmd/, and D2 about file naming follows the Go package convention from the planning constitution, so both are grounded in documented decisions rather than invented.\n\nThe task is self-contained with all the information the stitch agent needs—the format PRD, architecture details, use cases, and test suite—to implement the three source files within the 150-250 line target.\n\nLet me verify the line count estimate: size formatting around 40-60 lines, color output 60-80 lines, and column alignment 60-100 lines puts us solidly in the 160-240 range, which fits the constraint.\n\nOne thing to reconsider though—the required_reading field lists \"Find and read the PRD for pkg/format\" as a sentence rather than a proper file path, which doesn't match the spec for that field. I should either specify the exact PRD path or restructure how I'm listing the dependencies.\n\nI'm not certain of the exact PRD filename since they follow a pattern like prd[NNN]-format.yaml, so I'll keep it simple and just point to the directory where the stitch agent can locate it. And since go.mod already exists in the project structure, I don't need to create it—I just need to verify the pkg/format package is properly set up.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18480,"cache_read_input_tokens":16066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18480},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"797ec510-2818-4e4e-91e1-a8f1978035ae","uuid":"fcdaffdd-5469-44c4-89ab-b26f8ab35f8d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Qw4XrsUbVH3ip1qBVF4qTT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations built from documentation alone diverge in observable behavior, breaking scripts and pipelines. This project uses GNU utilities as a stress test for an AI code generation pipeline (mage-claude-orchestrator).\n\n**Architecture**: A four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify) produces Go implementations from C-source-derived PRDs. Key components:\n- `cmd/` — one Go package per utility\n- `pkg/sys/` — Darwin/Linux syscall abstractions\n- `pkg/format/` — shared output formatting (tables, colors, sizes)\n- `pkg/testutils/` — differential testing harness (compares Go binary vs GNU reference)\n- `magefiles/` — build orchestration (excluded from generation scope per DD7)\n- `docs/` — specifications (excluded from generation scope per DD7)\n\n**Current state**: All specs are written. Generated code (4,586 LOC) exists only at generation-merged tags — the working branch has no production code. All release 00.0 use cases have spec_complete status with code not started.\n\n**Current release (00.0)**: Foundational infrastructure batch. Four use cases remain:\n- uc001-magefiles (only cmd/version is a generation target; magefiles/ excluded by DD7)\n- uc002-format (pkg/format/)\n- uc003-sys (pkg/sys/)\n- uc004-testutils (pkg/testutils/)\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nAll three pkg/ packages are independent libraries at the same level — none depends on another. By P8 deterministic ordering: libraries before consumers, then alphabetical tiebreaker on primary file path. This yields: `pkg/format/` → `pkg/sys/` → `pkg/testutils/` → `cmd/version/`.\n\nWith a 1-task limit, the first task is **pkg/format/ implementation** (rel00.0-uc002-format).\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"pkg/format implementation -- size formatting, ANSI color, column alignment (rel00.0-uc002-format)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/format/ component -- responsibility and capabilities)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (locate and read the PRD for pkg/format; file matches pattern prd*-format*.yaml -- this PRD is the authoritative source for type names, function signatures, and API contracts)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc002-format.yaml (use case for format)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-00.0.yaml (test suite for release 00.0 -- format section)\n      - go.mod (module path and existing dependencies)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/size.go\n        action: create\n        note: Human-readable byte-size formatting (bytes to K/M/G/T/P/E units)\n      - path: pkg/format/color.go\n        action: create\n        note: ANSI color code output for file types and permissions\n      - path: pkg/format/column.go\n        action: create\n        note: Column alignment for tabular output (ls -l style)\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Implement human-readable size formatting that converts byte counts to\n          human-readable units (K, M, G, T, P, E), matching GNU coreutils output\n          conventions. Use the exact function signatures, rounding rules, and unit\n          thresholds specified in the pkg/format PRD.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Implement ANSI color code output for file types (directory, symlink,\n          executable, etc.) and permission display, supporting LS_COLORS environment\n          variable conventions. Use the type names and API contracts from the PRD.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Implement column alignment for tabular output in ls -l style, including\n          dynamic field-width calculation and per-column justification (left or\n          right). Use the alignment API and column type definitions from the PRD.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          pkg/format/ is a shared library consumed by multiple cmd/ packages\n          (ls, du, wc, etc.). It must not import from cmd/ or depend on any\n          utility-specific logic. Only Go standard library imports are permitted\n          (no golang.org/x/ dependencies).\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Each .go file is named after the primary capability it provides\n          (size.go, color.go, column.go), not after the package name. This\n          follows the project convention that the primary source file is named\n          after the primary exported type or capability.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/format/ succeeds with zero errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/format/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: |\n          pkg/format/size.go exports functions for byte-to-human-readable\n          conversion matching the signatures and behavior defined in the PRD\n      - id: AC4\n        text: |\n          pkg/format/color.go exports functions for ANSI color output\n          supporting file-type coloring per LS_COLORS conventions as defined\n          in the PRD\n      - id: AC5\n        text: |\n          pkg/format/column.go exports column-alignment functions for tabular\n          output with configurable per-column justification as defined in the PRD\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18480,"cache_read_input_tokens":16066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18480},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"797ec510-2818-4e4e-91e1-a8f1978035ae","uuid":"53a7fb64-90ce-45a0-9dd8-7cb6b00ce6cd"}
